{
  "_about": "Which Google Fonts subsets a composition loads for the market language, and the family it falls back to when its own font lacks them. Read by fonts.ts (the compositions) and engine/src/tm/video_fonts.py (the check before a render). A language (BCP 47, matched by its longest known prefix: zh-hant-tw, zh-hant, zh) maps to a script; unknown languages use latin. A script lists the subsets to load; a family that has all of them is used as it is, otherwise it draws the letters of the subsets it has and the script's fallback the rest (one font-family stack). A fallback split in numbered chunks (CJK) loads only the chunks tm render names in the props' fontSubsets. `families` lists the subsets and styles @remotion/google-fonts has for each family used (tested against the installed package).",
